  <running_head>Evangeli. Seculi. IV.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>6. Ac</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">tenus offertur ut hostia, non est in statu</l>
    <l n="2">exaltationis: destruit etiam natu-</l>
    <l n="3">ram humanam Christi, quod ex colla-</l>
    <l n="4">tione doctrinæ pontificiæ &amp; naturæ</l>
    <l n="5">humanæ Christi facilè intelligi poteft.</l>
    <l n="6" para="true">Et quia dato uno absurdo, alia se-</l>
    <l n="7">quuntur infinita, hinc tot <i>ἀτοπήματα</i>,</l>
    <l n="8">&amp; doctrinæ quæ maxima cum ignominia</l>
    <l n="9">&amp; contumelia gloriosissimi servatoris</l>
    <l n="10">nostri, coniunctæ sunt, obtinent in ec-</l>
    <l n="11">clesia Romana. Utpote</l>
    <l n="12">1. Transsubstantiatio dicitur etiam cum</l>
    <l n="13">substantia non mutatur in substantiâ.</l>
    <l n="14">2. Corpus non est circumscriptum.</l>
    <l n="15">3. Datur humanum corpus absq; forma</l>
    <l n="16">corporis.</l>
    <l n="17">4. Datur corpus quantum absq; quanti-</l>
    <l n="18">tate, longum absq; longitudine, visibi-</l>
    <l n="19">le absq; visibilitate.</l>
    <l n="20">5. Christus habet duo corpora, genitum &amp;</l>
    <l n="21">creatum.</l>
  </main_text>
